{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop","id":1025432,"title":"Devour the Slain, Knit endless loop.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-02T07:57:06-08:00","id":1025432,"title":"Devour the Slain, Knit endless loop.","content":"Here I am with another question.<br /> <br /> What, in game terms, would prevent a character that has Death 3/Life 3 from performing devour the Slain on himself and then using Knit to heal the damage, then rinse repeat to fill up on manna.<br /> <br /> Devour the Slain: Pull out 1 mana per potency and cause 1 lethal damage (not resistant lethal damage) in exchange. +1 reach doesn't count against the number of scours per day.<br /> Knit: With +1 reach heal 1 lethal damage per potency.<br /> <br /> Rinse and Repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:19:28-08:00","id":1025446,"title":"","content":"There's nothing there nothing stopping it, but I know that ultimately it's not that big a deal. I don't remember why exactly, because the last infinite loop thread was a while ago. I think it boiled down to, if it bugs you (or anyone else at your table) talk to your player. If that doesn't work you can make up a house rule to close the loop (Kind of lame imo, Mage is all about exploiting your sweet ass powers). Alternatively, if the player makes a habit of it then set up a scenario where it backfires on them. In the end you can also only do so much with infinite mana. Some of those things are pretty damn useful, but it's not like it's a game winning button smash technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:30:39-08:00","id":1025452,"title":"","content":"It was pointed out to me that I needed to read it a little closer, this is a two part denoted by the coma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening 2e, page 130</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For each level of Potency, the mage may take one point of Willpower (up to the subject\u2019s remaining Willpower points), or <b>he may Scour the subject\u2019s Pattern for one point of Mana</b>, <u><i><b>dealing one lethal damage in the process</b></i></u>, causing existing wounds to open and fester.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I did this on myself I would gain no mana as it is pulling from my body what I would be gaining. The wound is a byproduct of pulling it out, not what produced the mana. So in essence the subject goes down mana and I would go up the same amount, the subject would also take damage.<br /> <br /> Is that correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:47:51-08:00","id":1025459,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's a manipulation of the Scouring rules so it's not that you'd be draining mana from yourself for no net gain, you'd totally get that. It has to work that way because this spell can work on Sleepers when ty no mana in their Pattern except for what their Pattern is made of. What's interesting to me is that normally when you Scour the damage is Resistant, but in this spell it doesn't appear to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:50:10-08:00","id":1025462,"title":"","content":"Yes that is what I was looking at. I think it would totally work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:47:31-08:00","id":1025481,"title":"","content":"Now onto the morality of it. I can see that this kind of torture/conditioning tool could be considered a Left-Handed practice if used against another. However if s masochist were to do it to himself I do not see that as Left-handed. He could use it for religious purification, physical/emotional conditioning. He could be doing it because he feels that breaking down the body every so often and rebuilding it strengthens the body and soul.<br /> <br /> The question is would others find it Left-Handed in practice. even if he is doing it for altruistic reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:00:28-08:00","id":1025495,"title":"","content":"If he's not harming others by it then I don't see why they would be bothered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:09:09-08:00","id":1025497,"title":"","content":"I have a character that could do this Death 3 and Life 3, The ST stated that it can be done but repeated use could cause a new persistent condition and I can totally see that as you start to crave the pain. I think it is fair and adds drama to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:20:02-08:00","id":1025500,"title":"","content":"It also adds an opportunity for you to pick up more Beats, so there's literally no downside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:25:09-08:00","id":1025503,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that spell did Resistant damage, but maybe it doesn't because Resistant isn't intended to be something you can inflict on other characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:42:46-08:00","id":1025569,"title":"","content":"The lethal damage from Scouring is resistant. You can't heal it with Knit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:47:39-08:00","id":1025571,"title":"","content":"Even that done by the Spell Devour the Slain, it doesn't say that in the spell so Just checking. it specifically stated that it is 1 lethal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-02-2017, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:59:27-08:00","id":1025580,"title":"","content":"Well this leads me to another question. Assuming the damage done is meant to be Resistant Lethal, the page note explaining resistant damage specifies that it can't be healed through magic, though it doesn't specify that it only applied to <i>Awakened</i> magic. So if someone were to say, use the spell on a spirit and cause said spirit resistant lethal, could the spirit use its brand of magic (Numina) to heal its resistant lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:04:59-08:00","id":1025584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025569#post1025569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lethal damage from Scouring is resistant. You can't heal it with Knit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This means you could use Devour The Slain to inflict resistant lethal damage on enemies. No other 3 dot spells have this effect. Is this appropriate for a direct damage spell of the Death Arcanum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:05:53-08:00","id":1025585,"title":"","content":"I would not know but this just made the Devour the Slain one of the deadliest direct damage spells out there especially for being a 3 dot spell. Especially when you start to upgrade damage from lethal to aggravated from taking additional damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-02-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:51:51-08:00","id":1025600,"title":"","content":"Also the scour for mana causes 1 damage and you get 3 mana out of it. the spell doesn't give you 3 mana for one damage as a normal scour would. Sounds like the spell is working under special scour rules. This just opened alot more questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:46:22-08:00","id":1025626,"title":"","content":"Would it count under the self-mutilation Breaking Point for Wisdom? The example given is of creating a soul stone, but causing lethal damage to yourself for Mana seems to fit. At the least it seems like it would fit under Wisdom 8-10's 'using a spell to accomplish something she could do through mundane methods with little or no risk.' Also it's not exactly a free endless loop, as there's always going to be at least one Mana being used in the transfer, similar to getting Mana from a familiar. Unless you're of a legacy that gives Death and Life as Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> It seems like something you could do, but also seems like the kind of thing that would warp a mage. Conditions from Exceptional Successes or Dramatic Failures seem like they would lean towards the morbid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T17:05:58-08:00","id":1025631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025626#post1025626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it count under the self-mutilation Breaking Point for Wisdom? The example given is of creating a soul stone, but causing lethal damage to yourself for Mana seems to fit. At the least it seems like it would fit under Wisdom 8-10's 'using a spell to accomplish something she could do through mundane methods with little or no risk.' Also it's not exactly a free endless loop, as there's always going to be at least one Mana being used in the transfer, similar to getting Mana from a familiar. Unless you're of a legacy that gives Death and Life as Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> It seems like something you could do, but also seems like the kind of thing that would warp a mage. Conditions from Exceptional Successes or Dramatic Failures seem like they would lean towards the morbid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So... seems great on the surface, but leads to unintended consequences?<br /> <br /> Sounding more like a feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T17:38:04-08:00","id":1025642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025580#post1025580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this leads me to another question. Assuming the damage done is meant to be Resistant Lethal, the page note explaining resistant damage specifies that it can't be healed through magic, though it doesn't specify that it only applied to <i>Awakened</i> magic. So if someone were to say, use the spell on a spirit and cause said spirit resistant lethal, could the spirit use its brand of magic (Numina) to heal its resistant lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T23:44:40-08:00","id":1025755,"title":"","content":"Devour the Slain does resistant damage? That's a new one. Is the Willpower drain resistant too?<br /> <br /> Anyway, majority of the Infinite Mana Loop threads boil down to :yeah, it's possible, but not very convenient in middle of action, and regaining mana during downtime is already so easy that it's mostly used to say something about your character instead of being a real economic thing. Mana is supposed to be used, not hoarded; game encourages you to spent all your mana during the scene and then just regain it doing whatever when it's not interesting anymore. It's a resource that's interesting within a context of a single encounter, a tactical one; not a long-term strategic resource like Vitae. If mana would be hard to regain, people would just play passively and defensively around it being precious and rare, and that's rarely encourages interesting gameplay patterns. Like, if you can't reliably get your mana back, you will be less likely to blow all your Mana doing stuff, which means you will never encounter a situation where you have interesting choices of &quot;do I risk not using the mana here, or do I go full gonzo and burn it like candles&quot;?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Now I wonder if you can make someone &quot;Dead (Resistant)&quot; using Death Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T23:50:09-08:00","id":1025756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025585#post1025585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not know but this just made the Devour the Slain one of the deadliest direct damage spells out there especially for being a 3 dot spell. Especially when you start to upgrade damage from lethal to aggravated from taking additional damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really that good. It's resistant, but unlike other Direct Damage spells, you need to deal with Withstand. Giving someone 5 Resistant Lethal is cool, but un-resistable 9 Lethal will usually solve the problem better.<br /> It's funny that this spell became best way to cripple someone - cause a wound attached to a tilt, then reinforce it with Devour The Slain to make it annoyingly long and not-healable. Better than allmighty 4 dot Death Spells that just apply an Arm Wrack tilt. (Enervation sucks. Hard.)<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> If Devour the Slain literally scoures the pattern of the victim, can it scour the Paradox condition out of the target's pattern forcibly? Sounds like an interesting idea for Guardians. Kinda want to make a scene where abyss is integrated into some poor sleeper's pattern and only way to get it out is to scour their ass so hard they will almost die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-03-2017, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:25:17-08:00","id":1025774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025755#post1025755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devour the Slain does resistant damage? That's a new one. Is the Willpower drain resistant too?<br /> <br /> Anyway, majority of the Infinite Mana Loop threads boil down to :yeah, it's possible, but not very convenient in middle of action, and regaining mana during downtime is already so easy that it's mostly used to say something about your character instead of being a real economic thing. Mana is supposed to be used, not hoarded; game encourages you to spent all your mana during the scene and then just regain it doing whatever when it's not interesting anymore. It's a resource that's interesting within a context of a single encounter, a tactical one; not a long-term strategic resource like Vitae. If mana would be hard to regain, people would just play passively and defensively around it being precious and rare, and that's rarely encourages interesting gameplay patterns. Like, if you can't reliably get your mana back, you will be less likely to blow all your Mana doing stuff, which means you will never encounter a situation where you have interesting choices of &quot;do I risk not using the mana here, or do I go full gonzo and burn it like candles&quot;?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Now I wonder if you can make someone &quot;Dead (Resistant)&quot; using Death Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bBut that is the thing it isn't a true or full scour, If someone were to scour their pattern they would have the choice to scour a physical characteristic or take 1 point of resistant lethal damage, gaining 3 Mana in the process. With Devour the Slain you have the choice to take Willpower or take Mana, doing 1 point of damage. I would assume that the 1 point of damage is applied to taking willpower also, not sure anymore. So it is obviously not using the full scour rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025756#post1025756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really that good. It's resistant, but unlike other Direct Damage spells, you need to deal with Withstand. Giving someone 5 Resistant Lethal is cool, but un-resistable 9 Lethal will usually solve the problem better.<br /> It's funny that this spell became best way to cripple someone - cause a wound attached to a tilt, then reinforce it with Devour The Slain to make it annoyingly long and not-healable. Better than allmighty 4 dot Death Spells that just apply an Arm Wrack tilt. (Enervation sucks. Hard.)<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> If Devour the Slain literally scoures the pattern of the victim, can it scour the Paradox condition out of the target's pattern forcibly? Sounds like an interesting idea for Guardians. Kinda want to make a scene where abyss is integrated into some poor sleeper's pattern and only way to get it out is to scour their ass so hard they will almost die.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Withstand can also be gotten around, with relatively effective means. Still this means that there would be no battlefield healing this one.<br /> <br /> As to scour for paradox, maybe with a Reach, once again not sure anymore.<br /> <br /> My question is, do you have to heal damage from right to left, without skipping any boxes?<br /> <br /> Example if your health bar looks like this, <b>aggravated</b>, <b>lethal</b>, <b>lethal</b>, <b>Resistant lethal</b>. Do you need to heal the resistant before you can heal the other 2 lethal and then the aggravated? Does that one level of resistant lethal stop Knit from healing the 2 lethal between the resisted and the aggravated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-03-2017, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:59:44-08:00","id":1025786,"title":"","content":"Well, to add my opinion on Death damage spells being better... I think the Arcanum governing entropy, decay and destruction being better at killing people is a feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:20:17-08:00","id":1025812,"title":"","content":"It's not a very good arcanum for bringing harm to others. Fate Mage can break your leg using a 2nd dot spell that has multiple other options other than that, Death Mage will have to wait until 4th dot to be able to cast a spell whose sole and only purpose is to apply a Arm/Leg Wrack Tilt. It's Direct Damage spell has useless reach option for when you actually try to hurt someone.<br /> There was no reason to think that Devour The Slain does resistant damage either, as spell doesn't mention resistant damage at all and specifically states Lethal Damage.<br /> If Mage wanted to make a general rule that &quot;scouring&quot; always brings in &quot;resistant&quot; sacrifices, it failed to do so.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Random observation: You know what makes Obrimos fantastic Mage-Busters? Prime...AND Forces. Forces is fantastically unfair due to Control Heat spell; want to make enemy mage(s) crippled? Cast Control Heat with Potency of 4. People in the area will suffer penalty of four to all their rolls, which (probably? there is nothing stating it shouldn't) includes spellcasting rolls. <br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow Obrimos who turns up the heat and grapples you will make your spellcasting incredibly hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-03-2017, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:13:02-08:00","id":1025882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025774#post1025774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bBut that is the thing it isn't a true or full scour, If someone were to scour their pattern they would have the choice to scour a physical characteristic or take 1 point of resistant lethal damage, gaining 3 Mana in the process. With Devour the Slain you have the choice to take Willpower or take Mana, doing 1 point of damage. I would assume that the 1 point of damage is applied to taking willpower also, not sure anymore. So it is obviously not using the full scour rules.<br /> <br /> And Withstand can also be gotten around, with relatively effective means. Still this means that there would be no battlefield healing this one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What are these effective means? Right now I can really only remember the Praxis Nuke trick which isn't very effective for this spell, using victim's soul stone to bypass the Withstand and using Connected Sympathy to bypass Withstand. <br /> The thing about Praxis Nuke is that a lot of spells that can &quot;win&quot; the scenario are as effective at Potency 1 as they are at Potency 10. In such case, it's quite viable to leave the Potency at 1 and instead swing your massive dice pool of 9-14 dice and hope for 3 successes. You can do that with Devouring The Slain, sure, but...1 Damage DTS won't do you too much good. Only practical use I can see for this is when you have restrained a monster with big ass health pool and even bigger supernatural regeneration, so you decide to spam your Praxis to slowly kill it with resistant damage.<br /> <br /> Also, again, on Death being good at damaging people: your only mean of actually doing someone harm using Death spells pre-3rd dot is decaying random objects and hoping they will get hit by collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:22:40-08:00","id":1025886,"title":"","content":"Huh, the other Arcana <i>are </i>indeed just as good as wrecking people. Even better, at lower levels, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> shows. Then I give more weight to agreeing on Death being able to inflict resistant damage to make up for it.<br /> <br /> On healing damage with some of it being resistant as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> asks - dunno how the official rule goes, but I'd let non-resistant levels of the same damage type heal first, be it natural or with magic, but not let damage of the worse type heal before it. So in that example, the guy will heal 2 non-resistant lethal first, then the 1 resistant lethal, then the 1 aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:29:48-08:00","id":1025955,"title":"","content":"I think that this combo is better:<br /> <br /> this one<br /> <b>Vasalage</b>(Prime 3)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina<br /> When the Target of the spell Scours his Pattern all benefits that he would gain travels directly to the caster - or other specified Target.<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach</b> Target is no longer bound by daily restrictions<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach </b>every Scouring is refreshing and now gives 1 Willpower<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach</b> Scouring counts as an instant action (I couldn't find in the rules wether it is instant or reflexive so I made this effect to be sure)<br /> <br /> combined with<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Domination (</b>Mind2)<br /> &quot;Scour your pattern as long as you are able breath&quot; loaded with reach.<br /> <br /> <b>Combo Effect:</b> Your enemy slowly dies and you get steady supply of 3 mana per turn to fight with his friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-03-2017, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:37:04-08:00","id":1025960,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Devouring The Slain and then sending them back in time with Shifting Sands. Again, not for mana regeneration, but for putting your opponent in a situation where they are going to suffer damage over and over again as long as you keep putting them on repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:05:00-08:00","id":1025970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025882#post1025882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and using Connected Sympathy to bypass Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm missing some information this isn't possible. Connected Sympathy means that the sympathetic connection doesn't have a Withstand. All other Withstand ratings still apply. Multiple Withstand ratings takes the highest rating and adds one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:",