his Pattern all benefits that he would gain travel directly to the caster (Sovereign) - or other specified Target.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ 1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Target is no longer bound by daily restrictions</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ 1 Reach: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">every Scouring is refreshing and now gives 1 Willpower to Sovereign</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ 2 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> as above but for both Vassal and Sovereign</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ 1 Reach: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scouring is overwhelming and now counts as an instant action </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+ 2 Reach and 1 Mana:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sovereign can now once per turn reflexively demand a tribute from his Vassal in the form of Scouring</span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:22:53-08:00","id":1025980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025970#post1025970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I'm missing some information this isn't possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul stones proxy for their creators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:37:35-08:00","id":1025988,"title":"","content":"By having connected sympathy (i.e. you can't cast directly on the stone; you need to cast on the target via the stone and the Space 2 attainment) or is there something else in the book I'm missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:09:30-08:00","id":1026003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025988#post1025988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By having connected sympathy (i.e. you can't cast directly on the stone; you need to cast on the target via the stone and the Space 2 attainment) or is there something else in the book I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:18:26-08:00","id":1026010,"title":"","content":"But that doesn't bypass any Withstand on the actual target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:21:16-08:00","id":1026013,"title":"","content":"I..I am not sure, honestly. I don't use much Space Magic so I'm not very versed in ways of Sympathy. I was told many times that the main reason why someone having your Soul Stone sucks is because they can use this &quot;trick&quot; to bypass any Withstand you might have, basically leaving you at their mercy. If it isn't the case then, uh, Soul Stones dynamics change a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:33:04-08:00","id":1026025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026013#post1026013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I..I am not sure, honestly. I don't use much Space Magic so I'm not very versed in ways of Sympathy. I was told many times that the main reason why someone having your Soul Stone sucks is because they can use this &quot;trick&quot; to bypass any Withstand you might have, basically leaving you at their mercy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gives you a sympathetic Yantra and a sympathetic Withstand rating of 0. That's it. You still have to contend with their normal resistance-based Withstand ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:34:04-08:00","id":1026027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025882#post1025882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, again, on Death being good at damaging people: your only mean of actually doing someone harm using Death spells pre-3rd dot is decaying random objects and hoping they will get hit by collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spells given are not the sole capabilities of the arcana. I think you'd be able to at least partially replicate Control Heat and create an Extreme Environment with the Cold domain of Death. But most Arcana don't have a method to cause damage at one or two dots. You could probably pull off some sort of a death touch or chilling grasp, too, to enhance existing attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-03-2017, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:35:04-08:00","id":1026029,"title":"","content":"If 0 Withstand is still counted as a Withstand rating you might actually increase their Withstand rating anyway due to multiple Withstands. I doubt it works that way, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:24:22-08:00","id":1026108,"title":"","content":"I thinlk you are misreading devouring the slain. It's not a direct damage spell like the others. It's a willpower/mana generating spell. It let's you scour another living being, the damage is just part of the scouring and as such it's A SINGLE POINT of resistant lethal damage. Notice how the reach option for affecting Ghosts has a different wording.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:31:06-08:00","id":1026112,"title":"","content":"Notice the &quot;For each point of Potency&quot; part. If 5 points of Potency &quot;got in&quot;, you get to pick 5 times between reaping Willpower or dealing 1 Resistant Damage to generate 1 mana. So if you pick Mana 5 times, target is damaged for 5 resistant damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-03-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:59:14-08:00","id":1026151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025882#post1025882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What are these effective means? Right now I can really only remember the Praxis Nuke trick which isn't very effective for this spell, using victim's soul stone to bypass the Withstand and using Connected Sympathy to bypass Withstand.<br /> The thing about Praxis Nuke is that a lot of spells that can &quot;win&quot; the scenario are as effective at Potency 1 as they are at Potency 10. In such case, it's quite viable to leave the Potency at 1 and instead swing your massive dice pool of 9-14 dice and hope for 3 successes. You can do that with Devouring The Slain, sure, but...1 Damage DTS won't do you too much good. Only practical use I can see for this is when you have restrained a monster with big ass health pool and even bigger supernatural regeneration, so you decide to spam your Praxis to slowly kill it with resistant damage.<br /> <br /> Also, again, on Death being good at damaging people: your only mean of actually doing someone harm using Death spells pre-3rd dot is decaying random objects and hoping they will get hit by collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its primary factor is Potency so you can always reach for Advanced Potency, Someone with a Nimbus Tilt that reduces Resolve could force it into the world with a chance to affect the other person. You can always raise potency by taking negatives on the dice roll, like you said with the Praxis Nuke. Now granted they are all a gamble but they are options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:18:13-08:00","id":1026207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026151#post1026151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its primary factor is Potency so you can always reach for Advanced Potency, Someone with a Nimbus Tilt that reduces Resolve could force it into the world with a chance to affect the other person. You can always raise potency by taking negatives on the dice roll, like you said with the Praxis Nuke. Now granted they are all a gamble but they are options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the only purpose of Advanced Potency is to make a spell harder to dispel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:11:57-08:00","id":1026229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026207#post1026207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the only purpose of Advanced Potency is to make a spell harder to dispel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. Specifically, it gives you a +2 in the Clash of Wills roll for dispellation if I remember correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:55:28-08:00","id":1026247,"title":"","content":"Like I said I am new to the game, been playing 1 month today, and I may be misunderstanding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:33:48-08:00","id":1026358,"title":"","content":"No no no, Praxis Nuke is exactly NOT taking penalties. Here is how it goes:<br /> <br /> 1. Exceptional Success on a spell allows you pick an option from a list: one of these options is &quot;ignore Withstand&quot;.<br /> 2. Exceptional Success demands 5 successes, which is really hard to build for reliably.<br /> 3. Praxis, however, reduces that number to 3, making Exceptionally Succeeding reliable on pools of 9 and larger (I feel comfortable at 10 or 11)<br /> 4. There is a lot of spells that will work perfectly fine with Potency 1, and generally don't scale with it or scale poorly, instead using Potency to pierce Withstand. <br /> For example, Psychic Domination with Potency of 10 is as strong as Psychic Domination with Potency of 1. It's just that the P-1 version won't pierce any withstands.<br /> <br /> This means that, for certain spells, you are better off picking it at a Praxis and NOT spending dice on spellfactors. You usually leave everything at 1, conserving your spellcasting dice, and cover weaknesses with Reach (like, if spell would last 1 round, it's better for you to Reach for 1 Scene duration instead; if you need to target more than one target but less than 6 or you don't mind bombing the entire room, it's better for you to Reach for Advanced Area), and roll the massive dicepool. <br /> If you can assemble a dicepool of 9 dice for Praxis Nuke versus dicepool smaller or equal to 2 after getting the Potency needed to pierce the Withstand, you are better of Nuking.<br /> Same if you can get 10 dice and potency would take you to 3 or less. However, if you can get to &quot;4 dice after all the factors&quot;, normal casting starts looking better, even if you have larger Nuke Pools (diminishing returns). <br /> <br /> Damage Spells are good at what they do because they skip all of this nonsense and never are Withstood by anything. While your Devouring The Slain will lose 4 damage each time due to Withstand of the target, leaving you with pitiful 2 Damage per cast, Direct Damage spells will turbonuke the same target for 6 damage each time. This stacks really fast if you get two or more Mages deciding to &quot;fuck that guy&quot; and 100-to-0ing him in one round of spells .<br /> Still, outside of Direct Gangbang, damage spells are not the most efficient use of your time when you try to solve a violent scene. Or even when specifically trying to deal damage, which is where stuff like Forces and Matter using &quot;physics&quot; rules to do their dirty job rule the day.<br /> <br /> Now, I wonder...is Devouring The Slain considered a damage spell for purposes of Combining it with one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:12:12-08:00","id":1026529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026358#post1026358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I wonder...is Devouring The Slain considered a damage spell for purposes of Combining it with one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess so. But spellstacking rules apply for combining damage spells. So if you combine a potency 6 damage spell with Devouring The Slain against 4 Withstand, you will do 6 points of damage, two of them resistant and get the mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:11:03-08:00","id":1026618,"title":"","content":"I think I would rather combine it with some Stamina degrader, to decrease length of their health track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:02:46-08:00","id":1026643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026112#post1026112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice the &quot;For each point of Potency&quot; part. If 5 points of Potency &quot;got in&quot;, you get to pick 5 times between reaping Willpower or dealing 1 Resistant Damage to generate 1 mana. So if you pick Mana 5 times, target is damaged for 5 resistant damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't thibk that's the intended reading because it's incredibly better than any other damage spell. Not only is it stronger, which could make sense since it's Death, it also gives you mana. And if Death spells being better at damage was a design decision I think it would be mentioned in the Cretive Thaumaturgy section. I think the potency part only means you get more mana, but not aditional damage.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a mess of a spell, wether it's poorly worded as mana generation or poorly conceived as direct damage spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T13:45:11-08:00","id":1026670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026643#post1026643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't thibk that's the intended reading because it's incredibly better than any other damage spell. Not only is it stronger, which could make sense since it's Death, it also gives you mana. And if Death spells being better at damage was a design decision I think it would be mentioned in the Cretive Thaumaturgy section. I think the potency part only means you get more mana, but not aditional damage.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a mess of a spell, wether it's poorly worded as mana generation or poorly conceived as direct damage spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree because of the wording (See Below), <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA page 130</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For each level of Potency, the mage may take one point of Willpower (up to the subject\u2019s remaining Willpower points), or he may Scour the subject\u2019s Pattern for one point of Mana, dealing one lethal damage in the process,</div> </div> </div> </div>The <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;For each point of potency&quot;</span> is the qualifier and the <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;the mage may take one point of Willpower (up to the subject\u2019s remaining Willpower points), or he may Scour the subject\u2019s Pattern for one point of Mana, dealing one lethal damage in the process&quot;</span> is the result of each point of Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-04-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:35:14-08:00","id":1026695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\