trong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026670#post1026670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree because of the wording (See Below),<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;For each point of potency&quot;</span> is the qualifier and the <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;the mage may take one point of Willpower (up to the subject\u2019s remaining Willpower points), or he may Scour the subject\u2019s Pattern for one point of Mana, dealing one lethal damage in the process&quot;</span> is the result of each point of Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I think that's just poor wording. Compare it to Wither (Death 4), which is in line with all other direct damage spells, and thus much less powerful but still being one dot higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:15:00-08:00","id":1026715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026709#post1026709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, My apologies, I will choose a different color, is green or blue reserved for anything</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Annoying 10 character minimum</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:26:07-08:00","id":1026881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026670#post1026670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree because of the wording (See Below),<br /> <br /> The <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;For each point of potency&quot;</span> is the qualifier and the <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;the mage may take one point of Willpower (up to the subject\u2019s remaining Willpower points), or he may Scour the subject\u2019s Pattern for one point of Mana, dealing one lethal damage in the process&quot;</span> is the result of each point of Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>This...there's really no other sensible way to read the spell. I have a lot of gripes about wording with some of the 2E stuff, but this spell isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> It's not poorly worded at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:37:14-08:00","id":1026921,"title":"","content":"Again, it's not a Direct Damage spell and it's pretty bad at Direct-Damaging. Direct Damage spells don't care about Withstand, and can apply useful Tilts (Stunned is one of the best tilts you can do this way) guaranteed if you spend Reach. They are irresistable. <br /> <br /> Devouring the Slain, on the other hand:<br /> 1. Has to bear with Withstand, which makes it usually pretty much suck, as each point of Withstand costs you 2 dice to overcome, and you will end with pitifully low amount of damage compared to what you could do with the same dicepool using dedicated DD spells<br /> 2. Is limited to twice a day before forcing you to Reach for a permission to cast it at all!<br /> 3. Is limited to targets that have been hurt, and if you want to use it on someone who is healthy, it forces you to Reach.<br /> 4. It has no useful Tilt to apply.<br /> <br /> Ability to generate Mana is cool, but in combat it will be pretty useless. Why? Because you will need to spend so much Reach on this spell in any stress-inducing situation that you will have to burn more than you get in order to minimize Paradox. Lethal Damage is nice...but 6 Bashing is better than 2 Lethal. Why? Because massive Bashing will upgrade to Lethal quickly anyway, and filling someone's health meter with full bashing is desirable due to the fact that they might start having problems like wound penalties or, even better, being forced to check if they can stay conscious each round. This spell, unless in very specific circumstances, simply sucks as a Damage Spell. <br /> <br /> While Damage part of this spell is overrated, you know what's underrated? Willpower drain. Willpower drain is amazing, because Willpower is probably more valuable than Mana because it can boost your spellcasting by +3 and increase your withstand by +2, and while you still will effectively drain 1-2 Willpower points due to Withstand, it sucks much less than it being damage. Why? Because if you follow the guidelines for non-player characters and Willpower, most of them will have only one Willpower point per scene, and major characters - like, named enemy mages - will run with 2 or 3. <br /> <br /> If you are playing with Beaten Down rules, this spell is actually amazing at making use of Beaten Down. You can quickly Beat Down whole crowds by combining the Willpower drain and applying just 1 Lethal; 1 Lethal is enough to apply Beaten Down, and Willpower drain will take away any willpower they could use to take aggressive actions against you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:56:46-08:00","id":1026929,"title":"","content":"All good points, Do you do the damage for taking willpower also, or for just taking mana?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025774#post1025774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example if your health bar looks like this, <b>aggravated</b>, <b>lethal</b>, <b>lethal</b>, <b>Resistant lethal</b>. Do you need to heal the resistant before you can heal the other 2 lethal and then the aggravated? Does that one level of resistant lethal stop Knit from healing the 2 lethal between the resisted and the aggravated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still haven't received a reliable answer to this question. The reason it matters is to cap off damage that can be healed behind resistant damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T02:09:26-08:00","id":1026933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026929#post1026929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still haven't received a reliable answer to this question. The reason it matters is to cap off damage that can be healed behind resistant damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason to believe that a healing spell wouldn't just heal the types of damage it can. If Resistant acted as a blocker for healing normal damage, it would say so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T05:27:47-08:00","id":1026974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1025774#post1025774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example if your health bar looks like this, <b>aggravated</b>, <b>lethal</b>, <b>lethal</b>, <b>Resistant lethal</b>. Do you need to heal the resistant before you can heal the other 2 lethal and then the aggravated? Does that one level of resistant lethal stop Knit from healing the 2 lethal between the resisted and the aggravated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your health bar should never look like that in the first place. If your health bar looks like this: <b>aggravated</b>, <b>lethal</b>, <b>lethal</b> and then you get point of <b>resistant lethal</b> damage, I would upgrade the leftmost lethal to resistant and mark another lethal on the right. Rule goes &quot;Always mark the most severe injuries at the left of a character\u2019s Health track, and push any less severe injuries to the right. Characters heal their rightmost Health boxes first and progress left.&quot; I would use this for resistant damage, too.<br /> For the occasion that you really do heal the aggravated damage before the resistant lethal in this example, I would go with Inodiv.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 01-05-2017, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T06:02:19-08:00","id":1026985,"title":"","content":"I had asked earlier if resistant damage got pushed to the left of non-resistant of the same type and receive the answer that it should stay in the box it was marked in unless pushed by a higher class of damage. That is why I asked this question in the first place. And with the passage of <span style=\"color:blue\">Characters heal their rightmost Health boxes first and progress left.</span> I would say that you must heal the resistang damage first before moving on the the next box to the left, otherwise you are bypassing that rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T06:13:05-08:00","id":1026989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1026985#post1026985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had asked earlier if resistant damage got pushed to the left of non-resistant of the same type and receive the answer that it should stay in the box it was marked in unless pushed by a higher class of damage. That is why I asked this question in the first place. And with the passage of <span style=\"color:blue\">Characters heal their rightmost Health boxes first and progress left.</span> I would say that you must heal the resistang damage first before moving on the the next box to the left, otherwise you are bypassing that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's natural healing. Why are you assuming magical healing works the same way?<br /> If I have 2 agg and 3 lethal, and use a spell to heal agg, the lethal doesn't 'block' it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T06:47:51-08:00","id":1026997,"title":"","content":"Think of it less in game mechanical terms and more in what makes logical sense. If you got two stab wounds and a burn which is resistant to magic. Is there any logical reason, why you shouldn't heal the two stab wounds with a spell?<br /> The healing from right to left is meant for natural regeneration. It's also logical that a body gets rid of bruises much faster than of 3rd degree burns e.g.. And if you only heal naturally it doesn't matter where your resistant damage is anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:05:36-08:00","id":1027001,"title":"","content":"Fist you say look at these rules then it is but don't look at the rules, it needs to be one way or the other. And it say nothing in that or any other rule that I can find that the healing right to left is only for natural healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:50:05-08:00","id":1027024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1027001#post1027001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fist you say look at these rules then it is but don't look at the rules, it needs to be one way or the other. And it say nothing in that or any other rule that I can find that the healing right to left is only for natural healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is always &quot;read the rules and then use your own brain, too&quot;. There is nothing in the rules, that explicitetly says where resistant damage has to be marked, nor that it &quot;blocks&quot; any form of supernatural healing to non resistant wound. What is clearly stated is, that resistant wounds themselfs have to be healed via natural regeneration. There are multiple ways to do this in terms of how you mark your healthboxes and handle magical healing of other wounds. Pick whatever you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:55:42-08:00","id":1027027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA, page 223</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidebar<br /> <br /> Resistant Damage<br /> Some extremely rare effects cause resistant injuries \u2014 for mages they are almost always the result of containing a Paradox with Wisdom (see p.116). Resistant injuries are bashing, lethal, or aggravated like other wounds, <span style=\"color:Blue\">but the player should mark them with a dot above the Health box</span>. They cannot be healed by magic, or have their healing times accelerated by magic \u2014 only recovery at the rates on this page will work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right there is says that it should be marked so that you know where it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:02:15-08:00","id":1027032,"title":"","content":"The fact, that you know that you have resistant damage is not contratictory to the possibility of healing your non-resistant damage by magic. You mark it, so that you remember that you have resistant damage and not forget about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T11:59:36-08:00","id":1027193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop?p=1027001#post1027001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fist you say look at these rules then it is but don't look at the rules, it needs to be one way or the other. And it say nothing in that or any other rule that I can find that the healing right to left is only for natural healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire section it's found in is talking about natural healing. There's no basis to extrapolate that to magic that affects certain types of injuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-05-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}